  "published": "2026-08-25T17:54:46.19Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Utilities: moves the Platform_* permissions from 33-47 to 103-117. Security fix, upgrade immediately if you are on 26.8.25.1 or .2. Those two releases appended at the end of the enum SOURCE, but the enum is not the high-water mark - the database is. The enum once had 83 values (PHARMACY_*, OR_*, LIS_*) and commit 6dee40e of 2026-04-23 trimmed it to 19 without touching the data, so RolePermission still holds 1089 rows valued 48-102 and 325 more in 33-47. The new Platform_* values landed on top of them: the old PHARMACY_* block became PLATFORM_VIEW_TENANTS through PLATFORM_VIEW_PAYMENTS for 25 roles across 15 tenants, handing PLATFORM_APPROVE_DISCOUNT and PLATFORM_RUN_BILLING_CYCLE to 19 roles in clinics that never asked for them. 103-117 sits above every value the database has ever stored, and CreatePermissionBytes already skips values Enum.IsDefined rejects, so the stale rows go inert on upgrade with no data migration. Names are unchanged; only the numbers move. 33-102 are burned permanently - never assign there.",
